WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.620
When it comes to small screen couples, there
are virtually no rules as to who might hook

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.060
up with whom.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:11.809
Remember that time Tony Soprano slept with
his Russian mistresses' one-legged cousin?

00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:18.020
Or when the tough interrogator Sayid and the
spoiled rich girl Shannon became such a surprisingly

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.189
satisfying pair on Lost?

00:00:20.189 --> 00:00:25.339
Anything can and does happen when it comes
to TV romances, but that doesn't mean it's

00:00:25.339 --> 00:00:26.789
always okay.

00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:31.439
In the case of these on-screen couples, the
ick factor stemmed from their significant

00:00:31.439 --> 00:00:36.360
age differences, which made them nearly unwatchable
at times.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.150
Gloria and Jay

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:43.220
Though Modern Family has been credited with
breaking new ground on television, the romance

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:48.960
between Gloria and Jay has been accused of
retreating behind familiar stereotypes.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:55.040
Ed O'Neill's Jay was an aging businessman
who had a caustic relationship with his ex;

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:00.590
and Sofia Vergara's Gloria was a single mother
who was happy to take on the mantle of trophy

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:03.570
wife for the sake of financial security.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:08.350
"35 years we were together and he couldn't
wait 10 minutes to run off with Charo.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:10.250
That's a joke, joke.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.250
I'm kidding."

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:16.950
There's almost three decades of an age difference
between O'Neill and Vergara, and although

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:22.240
they have a good time working together in
real life, certain moments of romance between

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.170
the two can be a little unsettling to watch.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:27.939
"And it makes me uncomfortable."

00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:32.869
The redeeming factor of their relationship
is that the rest of the family has been allowed

00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:37.499
to mock the lopsided couple mercilessly over
the years.

00:01:37.499 --> 00:01:40.369
"I know what she thinks, a coal digger."

00:01:40.369 --> 00:01:42.040
"You know she's saying gold digger right?"

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.040
"YES, Phil!"

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:46.179
Carrie and Aleksandr Petrovsky

00:01:46.179 --> 00:01:50.769
The relationships portrayed on Sex and the
City could hardly be considered traditional

00:01:50.769 --> 00:01:54.479
— remember Samantha's naked sushi rejection?

00:01:54.479 --> 00:01:56.950
Yeah, it was a weird show.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:03.299
But in terms of uncomfortable age gaps, Carrie
Bradshaw took the cake with her strange patriarchal

00:02:03.299 --> 00:02:07.659
attraction to Aleksandr Petrovsky, the Russian
artist.

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:13.070
Bradshaw spent an entire series falling in
and out of love with men who were all wrong

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:16.910
for her, but Petrovsky was one of the worst.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:23.170
He was emotionally needy and distant at the
same time, and undermined her career achievements

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:26.530
for the sake of pumping his own ego.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:32.140
The fact that he treated her more like a neglected
daughter than a true partner made their age

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:35.520
gap that much more awkward to watch unfold.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.820
"I think you're acting like a child."

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:40.630
"And I think you're acting like an ---hole."

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:43.930
Detectives Andy Sipowicz and Connie McDowell

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:49.510
No matter the scenario, watching NYPD Blue's
Sipowicz get it on with Connie was always

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:51.570
going to be uncomfortable.

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:57.710
Beyond the relationship's physical mismatch,
the psychology behind it was also questionable.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:02.590
McDowell and Sipowicz bonded over her struggle
to reconnect with the daughter she was forced

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:08.440
to give up, as McDowell's maternal yearning
attracted her to Sipowicz, a grieving widower

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:10.510
and single dad to a young son.

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:14.250
Even the showrunners knew it would be hard
for audiences to swallow.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:19.720
Executive producer Bill Clark told the Los
Angeles Times that making Sipowicz and McDowell

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:23.510
hook up on the show was "like walking onto
a minefield."

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.000
"Think about something else.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.220
It'll pass."

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:28.950
Debra and Lundy

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:35.370
The unusual relationship between Debra and
Lundy on Dexter was actually pretty well-regarded

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:41.100
by fans who, at that point in the series,
were just ready for Deb to have any stable

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.100
relationship.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:47.810
Yes, Lundy was old enough to be her father,
and yes, he was sort of a superior officer,

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:53.760
but at least he wasn't secretly gift-wrapping
severed body parts and leaving them all over

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:54.760
Miami.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:56.020
That we know of.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:57.069
Hannah and Joshua

00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:03.650
HBO's Girls was brimming with bad relationships,
especially for Lena Dunham's leading character

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:04.650
Hannah.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:10.600
But while most of her hook-ups were age appropriate,
one episode portrayed her bizarre and unlikely

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:14.240
two-day romance with an older man named Dr.
Joshua.

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:19.850
The two got together after Hannah followed
him to his house, and they were in full horizontal

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:24.470
mambo mode within minutes -- with all the
deep talk between the two coming later.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:29.130
They split up almost as quickly as they got
together, but the idea that a middle-aged

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:35.840
doctor wouldn't hesitate to bed a twenty-something
with no notice was tired tripe, at best.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:37.220
Blanche and Dirk

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:42.720
Though she was the self-professed "man crazy"
one out of all of the roommates on The Golden

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:48.490
Girls, Blanche only had one romantic encounter
with a notably younger man.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:54.720
In one episode, Blanche, who has never revealed
her true age, was asked to dinner by her Jazzercise

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:59.760
instructor Dirk, and of course the awkward
conversations started flowing.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:04.660
Not only did he tell her she reminded him
of his mother, but Blanche's descriptions

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:08.520
of their torrid affair were especially unsettling.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:14.760
"I have decided to overlook that minor detail
and succumb to the Vesuvius of passion that

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.250
is about to erupt from me."

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:18.940
"Stand back, we're going to get something
on us."

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:24.630
That is as close to hearing your grandma describe
having sex as you'd ever want to get.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:25.630
Thanks for watching!

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:28.460
